WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.140
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit
7: Nature and the Environment.

2
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.240
Welcome to Unit 7!

3
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:12.860
In this unit you will explore the natural world — the
weather and the climate, the beach and the coast, forests,

4
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.920
mountains, and even our planet Earth.

5
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:21.860
You will learn to talk about places you have visited using
a new tense called the present perfect (“I have explored a

6
00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:22.260
forest”).

7
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:28.920
You will describe nature with colourful words, ask good
questions, and learn how to care for the environment.

8
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:36.340
By the end, you will be ready to go on a nature adventure
of your own, just like Adam and Amal in this unit's story.

9
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.260
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:47.920
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name and describe
places in nature: the beach, coast, forest, and mountain.

11
00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.660
you will also talk about the weather,
the climate, and the temperature.

12
00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:56.940
you will also say what you have done using
the present perfect: “i have seen the sea.”.

13
00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:59.480
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:05.720
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: climate,
weather, temperature, sunshine, froze, mountain.

15
00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:11.060
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

16
00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.600
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

17
00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:20.560
The reading sequence includes Our Wonderful
Nature and A Poem: “Nature Is Our Home”.

18
00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.320
Read actively.

19
00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.300
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

20
00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:31.420
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

21
00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:36.020
The first language focus is The Present Perfect Tense.

22
00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.640
We use the present perfect to talk about something
that happened in the past but still matters now.

23
00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:47.540
When you say “I have explored a forest,”
it shows this is part of who you are today.

24
00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.540
It helps you share your experiences with others.

25
00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:57.380
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

26
00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:03.020
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1 — Describe a Place in Nature.

27
00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:07.840
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

28
00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.900
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

29
00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:15.740
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

30
00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.480
You are ready to begin.

31
00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:24.260
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

32
00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:27.180
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

33
00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:32.680
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
